  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::BonePartInfo
  partName: Inbertebral DIscs
  partDescription: Flat, round cushioning pads located between the vertebrae. They
    act as shock absorbers to protect the spine and allow it to bend, twist, and
    move flexibly. Each disc has a tough outer ring (annulus fibrosus) and a soft,
    gel-like center (nucleus pulposus).
